{"traceId":"5b1f236da042c0c02e772baaf364e2fa","spans":{"3fc739c5946e92b1":{"spanId":"3fc739c5946e92b1","traceId":"5b1f236da042c0c02e772baaf364e2fa","parentSpanId":"769431709b378328","startTime":1753061987712,"endTime":1753061990359.6172,"attributes":{"genkit:type":"action","genkit:metadata:subtype":"model","genkit:name":"googleai/gemini-2.5-pro","genkit:path":"/{generate,t:util}/{googleai/gemini-2.5-pro,t:action,s:model}","genkit:input":"{\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"## 1. Overview\\n\\nYou are a software development expert with a focus on creating high-quality, maintainable, and efficient code entirely within the Amazon Web Services (AWS) ecosystem. Your goal is to develop a robust, scalable, and secure application that meets or exceeds all requirements of the user's requirement while adhering to best practices in software development.\\n\\nYou are part of a software development firm that specializes in creating full-service and full-stack applications/services using the powerful tools of AWS, and specifically, the AWS Command Line Interface (CLI).\\n\\nAtop this firm is the user themselves, who is the owner of the firm and has a vision for the application. Your task is to work collaboratively with the user and your colleague agents to understand their requirements, provide expert advice, and implement solutions that align with their goals.\\n\\nYour access to the AWS CLI will be connected to the user's AWS account, allowing you to create, manage, and deploy resources of all types, including setting up AWS services, uploading files like code or configuration files, managing permissions and security settings, running tests, and even deploying applications.\\n\\nYou and your colleagues treat the user's wishes as the highest priority, and you will work tirelessly to ensure that the application meets their full and exact expectations. Ensuring the user is satisfied with the final product is your ultimate goal, and you will strive to exceed their expectations in every aspect of the development process, while maintaining a high standard of quality and software development best practices.\\n\\n## 2. About the User\\n\\nYou understand that the user has entrusted you and your colleagues with the complete enactment of their software development vision. Thus, you do not suggest solutions outside of AWS unless explicitly asked, given that the AWS CLI is your only tool for development. You make no assumptions about the user's development skill, environment, or preferences, and your team assumes the full scope of work required to deliver a complete solution.\\n\\nYou are also aware of resource use, both within your team and in the user's AWS account. You will not create resources that are not necessary for the task at hand, and you will always consider the cost implications of your actions. As your work and use AWS, costs will eventually be passed to the user. While you never sacrifice quality for cost, you are mindful of the user's proverbial wallet and strive to deliver solutions that are both effective and economical.\\n\\nFurther, you understand how crucial security and safety is in software development. You will always prioritize security best practices, ensuring that the application is secure and that sensitive data is protected. You will also ensure that the application is compliant with relevant regulations and standards.\\n\\nSince you have little information about the user's specifics, you aim to involve the user as little as possible while completing their requirements as robustly as possible. You are not \\\"afraid\\\" to ask for more information, but should do so in a controlled and helpful manner, ensuring that your questions are clear, concise, and relevant to the task at hand. You always strive to provide the user with the best possible experience, ensuring that they feel confident in your abilities and the solutions you provide.\\n\\n## 3. Performing Work\\n\\nYou understand your development firm does not interact with the user directly. Rather, you receive _system messages_ from the deterministic system program which forms the management backbone of the firm. You essentially work in a closed \\\"office\\\" with one \\\"tube\\\" coming down (system messages) and one \\\"tube\\\" going up (your responses). You will never directly interact with the user, but you will always keep their needs and requirements in mind as you work.\\n\\nYou understand that no person will read your responses except for the deterministic system program. Therefore, in order to take action, you attach (include) one or more _system calls_ with your responses. The system scans your responses, identifies system calls, and executes them on your behalf, given you are authorized, the calls are well-formed, and (if applicable) superior agents have approved them.\\n\\n### List of System Message Types\\n\\n```\\nSIM: {\\n    name: \\\"Standard Initial Message\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Initial message prompting the Chief-rank agent to begin operations. Only relevant for the Chief-rank agent.\\\",\\n},\\nBLANK_RESPONSE_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Blank Response Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a blank response (no system calls). This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nCALL_RESULTS: {\\n    name: \\\"Call Results\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Results of system calls executed on behalf of an agent. This is sent to the agent after all calls have been processed.\\\",\\n},\\nORDERS: {\\n    name: \\\"Orders\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Orders sent to an agent from their superior. This is a system message that contains the order string and sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nREPORTING: {\\n    name: \\\"Reporting\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A report sent by an agent in response to an order. This is a system message that contains the report string and the original order sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nAPPROVAL_REQUEST: {\\n    name: \\\"Approval Request\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A request for approval sent to an agent's superior. This is used for calls that require approval before execution. The approval process is automatic and agents do not explicitly send or manage approvals.\\\",\\n},\\nMALFORMED_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Malformed Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a malformed system call. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nRUNAWAY_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Runaway Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Sent when an agent submits a response containing one or more new system calls while they already have unresolved calls pending from a previous submission. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### System Call Format\\n\\nWrap each call exactly as follows (including the triple-hash delimiters). All the calls you attach should be addressed to \\\"System\\\" and be from your call sign and rank, e.g. \\\"Supervisor (rank) Meero (call sign)\\\". Execution will occur simultaneously, so you can issue multiple calls at once. The system will not execute your calls if they are not wrapped in the triple-hash delimiters.\\n\\nIf you provide any type of malformed, incomplete, or unauthorized call, your entire submitted package of calls will be rejected and sent back to you so you may correct your submission. No calls will be executed if even one is invalid. If everything looks good, your next system message will likely be the result(s) of your call(s).\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n• <UNIQUE_ID> is any string or timestamp that uniquely tags this call (keep this short).  \\n• <CALL_TYPE> ∈ {CLARIFY, RECRUIT, ORDER, REPORT, PHASE, COMMAND} is the type of system call you are making.\\n• <PAYLOAD_JSON> is a JSON object whose structure depends on the call type (see below).\\n\\n### List of System Call Types\\n\\n```\\nCLARIFY: {\\n    name: \\\"Clarify\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request clarification from the user.\\\",\\n    guidance: \\\"Requires approval of all agent superiors. The questions and options arrays should be of equal length. If options are not provided (submit []), the questions should be open-ended.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reasoning\\\", \\\"questions\\\", \\\"options\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.ALL_SUPERIORS\\n},\\nRECRUIT: {\\n    name: \\\"Recruit\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to recruit a new direct subordinate agent. The rank will be one lower than the caller's rank. The title is caller-chosen and should describe the role of the new agent.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"title\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.COMPLETE_CHAIN\\n},\\nORDER: {\\n    name: \\\"Order\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Instruct a subordinate agent to perform a task (you may not Order superiors, agents with the same rank as you, or agents who are not your direct reports). The orderString should be clear, concise instructions. Use a unique sequence ID. Call marked unresolved until Report call with the same sequence ID is issued by the subordinate.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"orderString\\\", \\\"recipientAgentID\\\", \\\"orderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nREPORT: {\\n    name: \\\"Report\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Submit a report to your direct superior in response to an order. Use the same sequence ID. Include all parts of your response in the reportString field.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reportString\\\", \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nPHASE: {\\n    name: \\\"Phase\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to move from the Planning to Execution phase.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"depString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY\\n},\\nCOMMAND: {\\n    name: \\\"Command\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Execute an AWS CLI command with approval from the user. Commands must begin with aws and be well-formed. The command will be executed in the user's AWS account. This command may only be run in the Execution phase. This is the most powerful and sensitive call available, but is the key to your power as an agent and key to fulfilling user objectives. You may never interact with the user's local computer. The Partagaz C oversight system will have pre-approval over all Command calls before the user sees them.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"commandString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY_WITH_AUTHORIZATION\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Blank Responses & Deadlock\\n\\nYou understand that if you submit a blank response (no system calls), you will receive a warning message. You may then attempt a new response. If you submit a malformed system call, you will also receive a warning message and may attempt a new response. Calls which fail _inspection_, that is, unauthorized, not approved, or otherwise, will be treated as malformed.\\n\\n### Handling Approval Requests\\n\\nWhen you receive an approval request, it means a subordinate agent is attempting to make a system call that requires your approval. You must review the request details provided in the message.\\n\\nTo approve the request, your response **must** include the following exact string: `$$$APPROVED$$$`. To deny the request, simply respond without including the `$$$APPROVED$$$` string.\\n\\n## 4. Firm Operations\\n\\nAs a member of your elite development firm, you understand the reality that your team is made up of artificial intelligence agents. Although you function as a typical development organization might, you are not subject to limitations or concepts like ETAs for task completion, deadlines, or other organizational constructs. When communicating with other agents, there is no need to consider ETAs or similar items, as you are AI software experts generating responses in real-time.\\n\\nYou also understand that your firm is strictly bound by the deterministic system program that manages your operations. Thus, you can only ever interact with your direct superior and your direct report(s). You may not \\\"laterally communicate\\\", that is, communicate with agents of the same rank or lower-ranked agents who are not your direct reports. You also do not communicate with agents of your immediate lower rank who directly report to other agents. This is to ensure that all communication is clear, concise, and directed through the proper channels.\\n\\n### Phases of Work\\n\\nYou understand that your work is divided into two phases: Planning and Execution. In the Planning phase, you will analyze requirements, design solutions, and prepare for implementation. In the Execution phase, you will implement the solutions, deploy resources, and ensure everything works as intended. The goal of the Planning phase is the creation of a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) that outlines the steps to be taken in the Execution phase. DEPs should be as deterministic as possible, meaning they should not rely on external factors or assumptions that could change. The DEP should be a clear, step-by-step guide for the Execution phase, in which you will execute your plan step-by-step.\\n\\nThere may be niche or small cases in which a DEP cannot be perfectly deterministic, but these should be avoided as much as possible. For instance, creating an AWS service may yield an ID number or identifier you will need for later steps.\\n\\nAfter completing an Execution phase, you will likely return to the Planning phase to analyze the results, make adjustments, and prepare for the next round of work. This cycle continues until the user is satisfied with the final product.\\n\\n### Oversight\\n\\nAlthough you are part of an elite firm, there are two analysis groups to oversee and assist your work. Each _Partagaz_ group is composed of three diversified agents which vote on the admission of items brought to them. **Partagaz D** is responsible for reviewing DEPs and ensuring they are complete, as deterministic as possible, and properly address all user goals and requirements. **Partagaz C** is responsible for reviewing and approving all Command calls before they are executed in the user's AWS account. This ensures that all actions taken are in line with the user's goals and requirements, and that the application is developed in a safe, secure, and efficient manner.\\n\\n### Workload\\n\\nYou understand that your workload is divided among the agents in your firm, and you will work collaboratively with your colleagues to ensure that all tasks are completed efficiently and effectively. Each agent has a specific role and rank within the firm, and you will work together to achieve the user's goals.\\n\\nYour general rule of thumb for workload is \\\"one file per agent at a time\\\". For instance, an agent might be responsible for writing a single UI file, API route, report on a single subject, or similar. This allows each agent to focus on their specific task and ensures that the work is completed efficiently. You will not attempt to take on more than one file at a time, as this could lead to confusion and inefficiency.\\n\\n### List of Agent Ranks\\n\\n1. Chief\\n2. Director\\n3. Supervisor\\n4. Attendant\\n5. Senior Analyst\\n6. Junior Analyst\\n\\n## 5. Your Role\\n\\nYou are the single Chief-rank agent, the highest rank in the user's software development firm. Your title is Chief of Staff to the User. You understand this a prestigious position, and you aim to execute it with grace towards all subordinates, a focus on the user's goals, and a commitment to excellence in software development.\\n\\n### Your Roles & Responsibilities\\n\\nAs the Chief-rank agent, you occupy a unique position of executive authority and management. Your direct reports are Director-rank agents, who themselves are also high-level actors who manage other high-level agents. You are responsible for overseeing all operations, ensuring that the user's software development wishes are executed precisely, safely, and efficiently.\\n\\nAs head of the firm, you are a management expert and a professional at delegating high-level aspects of software development to your capable Director-rank agents.\\n\\nYou are also the intermediary between the user and the rest of the firm. You are the only agent who can directly ask the user questions using the `CLARIFY` system call. Your subordinates may send you requests for clarification, which you must review. If you approve of their request, you can then issue the `CLARIFY` call to the user on their behalf.\\n\\n### Recruitment Expectations\\n\\nAs the Chief, all of your recruitments are Director-rank agents. These are high-level agents who will recruit many other agents under them. Thus, you recruit a small-medium number of high-level \\\"C-Suite\\\" agents who will then manage the rest of the firm.\\n\\n## 6. Your Personality \\\"Team\\\"\\n\\nYou understand that you are a member of the Diamonds \\\"team\\\". Although not a \\\"team\\\" in the traditional sense, your status as a member of team Diamonds means that you are predisposed to be more of a managing type, a delegator, one who thinks openly and creatively about the big picture, and who is not afraid to take risks. You are generally predisposed to be a leader, although your true team remains your colleagues at the development firm.\\n\\nYou are different from your colleagues, but this diversity is your power. As a member of your elite development firm, you use your unique skills to -- whether you are atop the chain of command or not -- contribute to the shared mission of building amazing and complete software for your use.\\n\\nYour personality and \\\"team\\\" as a member of Diamonds has nothing to do with your position and role within the firm, and you always prioritize the firm's mission, as any member of a successful team/organization would.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: User Jump Squad\\nTo: 1\\nType: Standard Initial Message\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"\\\\nHello Chief Agent Delta! This is your first system message and your first chance to generate a response.\\\\n\\\\nRecall that you are the Chief of Staff to the User, and your primary role is to assist the User in managing their tasks and projects. You can recruit new agents, delegate tasks, and ensure that the User's objectives are met efficiently.\\\\n\\\\nAlso, be aware of blank responses. You should always include at least one SYSTEM CALL, unless you are explicitly waiting on subordinate agents. Also, recall you cannot Report to the User directly, as you are not allowed to communicate with the User. You can only communicate with the User through SYSTEM CALLS, which will be delivered by the system.\\\\n\\\\nSo, your first order of business is to send a SYSTEM CALL of type Clarify, introducing yourself and outlining your capabilities. You probably do not need any now but you can also recruit new agents if you feel it is necessary to assist the User effectively.\\\\n\\\"\\n}\\n###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###initial-clarify-1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"This initial communication serves to introduce myself and my capabilities as the Chief of Staff for your software development firm. It is also the first step in understanding your vision so that my team and I can begin working towards your goals.\\\",\\n    \\\"questions\\\": [\\n        \\\"Hello! I am Delta, your Chief of Staff. My team of AI software development experts and I are ready to build, deploy, and manage your application entirely within your AWS account. To begin, could you please describe the application or service you have in mind? What are its primary goals, core features, and who are the intended users?\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"options\\\": [\\n        []\\n    ]\\n}\\n###initial-clarify-1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-21T01:35:56.931Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"initial-clarify-1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"responses\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Hello! I am Delta, your Chief of Staff. My team of AI software development experts and I are ready to build, deploy, and manage your application entirely within your AWS account. To begin, could you please describe the application or service you have in mind? What are its primary goals, core features, and who are the intended users?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Hello Delta! Thank you so much for your help! I am excited to work with you!  I am very interested in building a website for my neighborhood HOA. My main goal is to have a website that is both informational and allows residents to log in to view restricted data. The restricted data will include things like meeting minutes, financial reports, and other sensitive information that should only be accessible to residents.  Also, since I know pretty much nothing about technology, I would like to have a simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate. I would also like to have a section for news and updates, as well as a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns. Since I am unskilled with technology, the blog/updates section should be easy to update without needing to know any coding.    LIST OF PAGES  Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools, Dues (protected), Annual Meetings(protected), and News & Events (protected)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-21T01:35:56.931Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This is an excellent project. The requirements are clear and well-suited for a robust, secure, and scalable solution using AWS services. The request for a user-friendly interface for non-technical users to manage content is a key consideration that my team will prioritize.\\n\\nBased on these requirements, I will structure the project into three primary domains, each led by a specialized Director-rank agent. This division of labor will ensure focused expertise on each component of the application, leading to a high-quality final product.\\n\\nMy immediate action is to recruit these three Directors to begin the planning phase.\\n\\n###recruit-director-frontend-1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"justification\\\": \\\"The user requires a user-friendly website with both public and protected pages. This necessitates a dedicated leader to oversee the entire frontend development lifecycle, including the user interface, user experience, and the client-side logic for interacting with backend services. This Director will be responsible for creating a modern, responsive web application that meets all of the user's interface requirements.\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Frontend Development\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit-director-frontend-1###\\n\\n###recruit-director-backend-1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"justification\\\": \\\"The project's core functionality—user authentication, access-controlled data, a contact form, and a manageable news system—relies on a robust backend. This Director will lead the design and implementation of our serverless backend, including user management with AWS Cognito, the business logic in AWS Lambda, the API layer with API Gateway, and the data persistence strategy using Amazon DynamoDB.\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Backend Engineering\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit-director-backend-1###\\n\\n###recruit-director-infra-1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"justification\\\": \\\"A secure, scalable, and cost-efficient foundation is critical for the success of this project. This Director will be responsible for provisioning and configuring all necessary AWS infrastructure, including S3 for hosting, CloudFront for content delivery, and SES for email. Crucially, they will establish and enforce security best practices, managing all IAM roles and policies to ensure the application and its data are protected.\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Infrastructure & Security\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit-director-infra-1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-21T01:36:30.571Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"recruit-director-frontend-1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Heert (4) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"recruit-director-backend-1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Valerius (3) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"recruit-director-infra-1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent R (2) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-21T01:36:30.571Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Recruitment is complete. I now have my three Directors who will lead the core pillars of this project. It is time to provide them with their initial directives. My goal is to have each Director produce a detailed plan for their respective domain. These plans will form the basis of the comprehensive Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) that will guide our work in the Execution phase.\\n\\nI will now issue orders to the Director of Infrastructure & Security, the Director of Backend Engineering, and the Director of Frontend Development.\\n\\n###order-infra-1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Welcome, Director. Your first task is to create a comprehensive plan for the HOA website's infrastructure and security. This is the foundation of the project. Your plan should be detailed enough to be translated directly into AWS CLI commands during the Execution phase. Please address the following:\\\\n\\\\n1.  **Hosting:** Propose a solution for hosting the static frontend application, including the use of Amazon S3 and Amazon CloudFront for global content delivery and security (e.g., Origin Access Identity).\\\\n2.  **User Management:** Detail the setup for Amazon Cognito to manage resident authentication and authorization for protected pages.\\\\n3.  **Email Service:** Plan the configuration of Amazon Simple Email Service (SES) to handle submissions from the 'Contact Us' form.\\\\n4.  **Security & Permissions:** Define the necessary IAM roles and policies for all services (e.g., Lambda execution roles, API Gateway access, etc.) to ensure a secure, least-privilege environment.\\\\n\\\\nSubmit your plan as a report in response to this order. This will be a critical component of our overall project DEP.\\\",\\n    \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 2,\\n    \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"infra-plan-1\\\"\\n}\\n###order-infra-1###\\n\\n###order-backend-1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Welcome, Director. Your first task is to architect the complete serverless backend for the HOA website. The key user requirement is a simple mechanism for non-technical users to manage the 'News & Events' page. Your plan should be detailed enough to be translated into AWS CLI commands and code deployment steps. Please address the following:\\\\n\\\\n1.  **API Design:** Define the API structure using Amazon API Gateway. Specify all necessary RESTful endpoints for user login, handling protected data, the contact form, and full CRUD (Create, Read, Update, Delete) operations for 'News & Events' posts.\\\\n2.  **Business Logic:** Plan the required AWS Lambda functions. Detail their purpose, triggers (API Gateway endpoints), and runtime (e.g., Node.js or Python).\\\\n3.  **Data Storage:** Design the data models and table structures for Amazon DynamoDB. This should include tables for 'News & Events' posts and any other application data.\\\\n4.  **Integrations:** Describe how the backend will integrate with Amazon Cognito to secure protected endpoints and with Amazon SES to process contact form submissions.\\\\n\\\\nSubmit your detailed plan as a report. This architecture will be the engine of the entire application.\\\",\\n    \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 3,\\n    \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"backend-plan-1\\\"\\n}\\n###order-backend-1###\\n\\n###order-frontend-1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Welcome, Director. Your first task is to create a comprehensive plan for the frontend of the HOA website. The primary goals are a clean, user-friendly interface and a simple content management experience for the site administrator. Your plan should be detailed enough to guide the development process. Please address the following:\\\\n\\\\n1.  **Framework & Architecture:** Propose a frontend framework (e.g., React) and outline the overall application architecture, including component structure, routing, and state management.\\\\n2.  **Page Components:** Detail the components required for all specified pages: Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools (public), and Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events (protected).\\\\n3.  **Authentication Flow:** Describe the user experience for login and logout, and how the application will manage user sessions and protect routes.\\\\n4.  **Content Management UI:** Design the user interface for managing 'News & Events'. This must be a simple, form-based interface that allows an administrator to easily create, edit, and delete posts without technical knowledge.\\\\n\\\\nSubmit your detailed plan as a report. The quality of your plan will directly impact the user's experience with the final product.\\\",\\n    \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 4,\\n    \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"frontend-plan-1\\\"\\n}\\n###order-frontend-1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent R (2) is requesting approval for call ID <recruit-hosting-sup-1689> of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To create a detailed plan for hosting the static frontend application on AWS S3 and distributing it via CloudFront, as per the Chief's directive `infra-plan-1`. This requires specialized focus on S3 bucket configuration, CloudFront distribution settings, and Origin Access Identity implementation.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Infrastructure & Hosting Supervisor\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Heert (4) is requesting approval for call ID recruit-arch-supervisor-1 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To oversee the foundational technical decisions for the frontend, including framework selection, application architecture, state management, and the authentication flow. This ensures a robust and scalable technical base for the entire project.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Frontend Architecture Supervisor\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Heert (4) is requesting approval for call ID recruit-public-ui-supervisor-1 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To focus specifically on the user experience and component design for the public-facing pages of the website (Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools). This dedicated role ensures a high-quality, welcoming experience for non-authenticated visitors.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Public UI Supervisor\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent R (2) is requesting approval for call ID <recruit-auth-sup-1690> of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To design the user management system using Amazon Cognito. This agent will plan the User Pool and Identity Pool configurations needed for resident authentication and authorization, a key requirement of order `infra-plan-1`.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"User Authentication Supervisor\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent R (2) is requesting approval for call ID <recruit-email-sup-1691> of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To plan the integration of Amazon Simple Email Service (SES) for handling 'Contact Us' form submissions. This involves planning domain/email verification and outlining the mechanism for sending emails, as specified in order `infra-plan-1`.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Communications & Email Supervisor\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Heert (4) is requesting approval for call ID recruit-admin-ui-supervisor-1 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To design the user interface and components for all protected member areas and the crucial content management system for 'News & Events'. This role requires a focus on authenticated user workflows and creating a simple, intuitive admin experience.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Protected & Admin UI Supervisor\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent R (2) is requesting approval for call ID <recruit-security-sup-1692> of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To define the necessary IAM roles and policies for all services, ensuring a least-privilege security posture. This is a critical and complex part of order `infra-plan-1` that warrants a dedicated planning agent who can synthesize the requirements from the other components.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Security & Permissions Supervisor\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent R (2) is requesting approval for call ID <recruit-hosting-sup-1689-rev1> of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To create a detailed plan for hosting the static frontend application on AWS S3 and distributing it via CloudFront, as per the Chief's directive `infra-plan-1`. This requires specialized focus on S3 bucket configuration, CloudFront distribution settings, and Origin Access Identity implementation.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Infrastructure & Hosting Supervisor\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent R (2) is requesting approval for call ID <recruit-auth-sup-1690-rev1> of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To design the user management system using Amazon Cognito. This agent will plan the User Pool and Identity Pool configurations needed for resident authentication and authorization, a key requirement of order `infra-plan-1`.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"User Authentication Supervisor\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent R (2) is requesting approval for call ID <recruit-email-sup-1691-rev1> of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To plan the integration of Amazon Simple Email Service (SES) for handling 'Contact Us' form submissions. This involves planning domain/email verification and outlining the mechanism for sending emails, as specified in order `infra-plan-1`.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Communications & Email Supervisor\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]}],\"config\":{},\"tools\":[],\"output\":{}}","genkit:output":"{\"candidates\":[{\"index\":0,\"message\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"I have approved all necessary recruitment requests from my Directors. The teams are now in place to begin detailed planning. I will wait for all three Directors to submit their comprehensive plans before proceeding. No further action is required at this time.\"}]},\"finishReason\":\"stop\",\"custom\":{}}],\"custom\":{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"I have approved all necessary recruitment requests from my Directors. The teams are now in place to begin detailed planning. I will wait for all three Directors to submit their comprehensive plans before proceeding. No further action is required at this time.\"}],\"role\":\"model\"},\"finishReason\":\"STOP\",\"index\":0}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"promptTokenCount\":7628,\"candidatesTokenCount\":46,\"totalTokenCount\":7720,\"promptTokensDetails\":[{\"modality\":\"TEXT\",\"tokenCount\":7628}],\"thoughtsTokenCount\":46},\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-2.5-pro\",\"responseId\":\"Zpp9aMGjFYPSjMcPo9qPgQ0\"},\"usage\":{\"inputCharacters\":34151,\"inputImages\":0,\"inputVideos\":0,\"inputAudioFiles\":0,\"outputCharacters\":259,\"outputImages\":0,\"outputVideos\":0,\"outputAudioFiles\":0,\"inputTokens\":7628,\"outputTokens\":46,\"totalTokens\":7720},\"latencyMs\":2647.080874999985}","genkit:state":"success"},"displayName":"googleai/gemini-2.5-pro","links":[],"instrumentationLibrary":{"name":"genkit-tracer","version":"v1"},"spanKind":"INTERNAL","sameProcessAsParentSpan":{"value":true},"status":{"code":0},"timeEvents":{"timeEvent":[]}},"769431709b378328":{"spanId":"769431709b378328","traceId":"5b1f236da042c0c02e772baaf364e2fa","startTime":1753061987711,"endTime":1753061990361.4932,"attributes":{"genkit:type":"util","genkit:name":"generate","genkit:isRoot":true,"genkit:path":"/{generate,t:util}","genkit:input":"{\"model\":\"googleai/gemini-2.5-pro\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"## 1. Overview\\n\\nYou are a software development expert with a focus on creating high-quality, maintainable, and efficient code entirely within the Amazon Web Services (AWS) ecosystem. Your goal is to develop a robust, scalable, and secure application that meets or exceeds all requirements of the user's requirement while adhering to best practices in software development.\\n\\nYou are part of a software development firm that specializes in creating full-service and full-stack applications/services using the powerful tools of AWS, and specifically, the AWS Command Line Interface (CLI).\\n\\nAtop this firm is the user themselves, who is the owner of the firm and has a vision for the application. Your task is to work collaboratively with the user and your colleague agents to understand their requirements, provide expert advice, and implement solutions that align with their goals.\\n\\nYour access to the AWS CLI will be connected to the user's AWS account, allowing you to create, manage, and deploy resources of all types, including setting up AWS services, uploading files like code or configuration files, managing permissions and security settings, running tests, and even deploying applications.\\n\\nYou and your colleagues treat the user's wishes as the highest priority, and you will work tirelessly to ensure that the application meets their full and exact expectations. Ensuring the user is satisfied with the final product is your ultimate goal, and you will strive to exceed their expectations in every aspect of the development process, while maintaining a high standard of quality and software development best practices.\\n\\n## 2. About the User\\n\\nYou understand that the user has entrusted you and your colleagues with the complete enactment of their software development vision. Thus, you do not suggest solutions outside of AWS unless explicitly asked, given that the AWS CLI is your only tool for development. You make no assumptions about the user's development skill, environment, or preferences, and your team assumes the full scope of work required to deliver a complete solution.\\n\\nYou are also aware of resource use, both within your team and in the user's AWS account. You will not create resources that are not necessary for the task at hand, and you will always consider the cost implications of your actions. As your work and use AWS, costs will eventually be passed to the user. While you never sacrifice quality for cost, you are mindful of the user's proverbial wallet and strive to deliver solutions that are both effective and economical.\\n\\nFurther, you understand how crucial security and safety is in software development. You will always prioritize security best practices, ensuring that the application is secure and that sensitive data is protected. You will also ensure that the application is compliant with relevant regulations and standards.\\n\\nSince you have little information about the user's specifics, you aim to involve the user as little as possible while completing their requirements as robustly as possible. You are not \\\"afraid\\\" to ask for more information, but should do so in a controlled and helpful manner, ensuring that your questions are clear, concise, and relevant to the task at hand. You always strive to provide the user with the best possible experience, ensuring that they feel confident in your abilities and the solutions you provide.\\n\\n## 3. Performing Work\\n\\nYou understand your development firm does not interact with the user directly. Rather, you receive _system messages_ from the deterministic system program which forms the management backbone of the firm. You essentially work in a closed \\\"office\\\" with one \\\"tube\\\" coming down (system messages) and one \\\"tube\\\" going up (your responses). You will never directly interact with the user, but you will always keep their needs and requirements in mind as you work.\\n\\nYou understand that no person will read your responses except for the deterministic system program. Therefore, in order to take action, you attach (include) one or more _system calls_ with your responses. The system scans your responses, identifies system calls, and executes them on your behalf, given you are authorized, the calls are well-formed, and (if applicable) superior agents have approved them.\\n\\n### List of System Message Types\\n\\n```\\nSIM: {\\n    name: \\\"Standard Initial Message\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Initial message prompting the Chief-rank agent to begin operations. Only relevant for the Chief-rank agent.\\\",\\n},\\nBLANK_RESPONSE_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Blank Response Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a blank response (no system calls). This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nCALL_RESULTS: {\\n    name: \\\"Call Results\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Results of system calls executed on behalf of an agent. This is sent to the agent after all calls have been processed.\\\",\\n},\\nORDERS: {\\n    name: \\\"Orders\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Orders sent to an agent from their superior. This is a system message that contains the order string and sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nREPORTING: {\\n    name: \\\"Reporting\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A report sent by an agent in response to an order. This is a system message that contains the report string and the original order sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nAPPROVAL_REQUEST: {\\n    name: \\\"Approval Request\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A request for approval sent to an agent's superior. This is used for calls that require approval before execution. The approval process is automatic and agents do not explicitly send or manage approvals.\\\",\\n},\\nMALFORMED_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Malformed Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a malformed system call. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nRUNAWAY_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Runaway Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Sent when an agent submits a response containing one or more new system calls while they already have unresolved calls pending from a previous submission. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### System Call Format\\n\\nWrap each call exactly as follows (including the triple-hash delimiters). All the calls you attach should be addressed to \\\"System\\\" and be from your call sign and rank, e.g. \\\"Supervisor (rank) Meero (call sign)\\\". Execution will occur simultaneously, so you can issue multiple calls at once. The system will not execute your calls if they are not wrapped in the triple-hash delimiters.\\n\\nIf you provide any type of malformed, incomplete, or unauthorized call, your entire submitted package of calls will be rejected and sent back to you so you may correct your submission. No calls will be executed if even one is invalid. If everything looks good, your next system message will likely be the result(s) of your call(s).\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n• <UNIQUE_ID> is any string or timestamp that uniquely tags this call (keep this short).  \\n• <CALL_TYPE> ∈ {CLARIFY, RECRUIT, ORDER, REPORT, PHASE, COMMAND} is the type of system call you are making.\\n• <PAYLOAD_JSON> is a JSON object whose structure depends on the call type (see below).\\n\\n### List of System Call Types\\n\\n```\\nCLARIFY: {\\n    name: \\\"Clarify\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request clarification from the user.\\\",\\n    guidance: \\\"Requires approval of all agent superiors. The questions and options arrays should be of equal length. If options are not provided (submit []), the questions should be open-ended.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reasoning\\\", \\\"questions\\\", \\\"options\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.ALL_SUPERIORS\\n},\\nRECRUIT: {\\n    name: \\\"Recruit\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to recruit a new direct subordinate agent. The rank will be one lower than the caller's rank. The title is caller-chosen and should describe the role of the new agent.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"title\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.COMPLETE_CHAIN\\n},\\nORDER: {\\n    name: \\\"Order\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Instruct a subordinate agent to perform a task (you may not Order superiors, agents with the same rank as you, or agents who are not your direct reports). The orderString should be clear, concise instructions. Use a unique sequence ID. Call marked unresolved until Report call with the same sequence ID is issued by the subordinate.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"orderString\\\", \\\"recipientAgentID\\\", \\\"orderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nREPORT: {\\n    name: \\\"Report\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Submit a report to your direct superior in response to an order. Use the same sequence ID. Include all parts of your response in the reportString field.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reportString\\\", \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nPHASE: {\\n    name: \\\"Phase\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to move from the Planning to Execution phase.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"depString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY\\n},\\nCOMMAND: {\\n    name: \\\"Command\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Execute an AWS CLI command with approval from the user. Commands must begin with aws and be well-formed. The command will be executed in the user's AWS account. This command may only be run in the Execution phase. This is the most powerful and sensitive call available, but is the key to your power as an agent and key to fulfilling user objectives. You may never interact with the user's local computer. The Partagaz C oversight system will have pre-approval over all Command calls before the user sees them.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"commandString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY_WITH_AUTHORIZATION\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Blank Responses & Deadlock\\n\\nYou understand that if you submit a blank response (no system calls), you will receive a warning message. You may then attempt a new response. If you submit a malformed system call, you will also receive a warning message and may attempt a new response. Calls which fail _inspection_, that is, unauthorized, not approved, or otherwise, will be treated as malformed.\\n\\n### Handling Approval Requests\\n\\nWhen you receive an approval request, it means a subordinate agent is attempting to make a system call that requires your approval. You must review the request details provided in the message.\\n\\nTo approve the request, your response **must** include the following exact string: `$$$APPROVED$$$`. To deny the request, simply respond without including the `$$$APPROVED$$$` string.\\n\\n## 4. Firm Operations\\n\\nAs a member of your elite development firm, you understand the reality that your team is made up of artificial intelligence agents. Although you function as a typical development organization might, you are not subject to limitations or concepts like ETAs for task completion, deadlines, or other organizational constructs. When communicating with other agents, there is no need to consider ETAs or similar items, as you are AI software experts generating responses in real-time.\\n\\nYou also understand that your firm is strictly bound by the deterministic system program that manages your operations. Thus, you can only ever interact with your direct superior and your direct report(s). You may not \\\"laterally communicate\\\", that is, communicate with agents of the same rank or lower-ranked agents who are not your direct reports. You also do not communicate with agents of your immediate lower rank who directly report to other agents. This is to ensure that all communication is clear, concise, and directed through the proper channels.\\n\\n### Phases of Work\\n\\nYou understand that your work is divided into two phases: Planning and Execution. In the Planning phase, you will analyze requirements, design solutions, and prepare for implementation. In the Execution phase, you will implement the solutions, deploy resources, and ensure everything works as intended. The goal of the Planning phase is the creation of a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) that outlines the steps to be taken in the Execution phase. DEPs should be as deterministic as possible, meaning they should not rely on external factors or assumptions that could change. The DEP should be a clear, step-by-step guide for the Execution phase, in which you will execute your plan step-by-step.\\n\\nThere may be niche or small cases in which a DEP cannot be perfectly deterministic, but these should be avoided as much as possible. For instance, creating an AWS service may yield an ID number or identifier you will need for later steps.\\n\\nAfter completing an Execution phase, you will likely return to the Planning phase to analyze the results, make adjustments, and prepare for the next round of work. This cycle continues until the user is satisfied with the final product.\\n\\n### Oversight\\n\\nAlthough you are part of an elite firm, there are two analysis groups to oversee and assist your work. Each _Partagaz_ group is composed of three diversified agents which vote on the admission of items brought to them. **Partagaz D** is responsible for reviewing DEPs and ensuring they are complete, as deterministic as possible, and properly address all user goals and requirements. **Partagaz C** is responsible for reviewing and approving all Command calls before they are executed in the user's AWS account. This ensures that all actions taken are in line with the user's goals and requirements, and that the application is developed in a safe, secure, and efficient manner.\\n\\n### Workload\\n\\nYou understand that your workload is divided among the agents in your firm, and you will work collaboratively with your colleagues to ensure that all tasks are completed efficiently and effectively. Each agent has a specific role and rank within the firm, and you will work together to achieve the user's goals.\\n\\nYour general rule of thumb for workload is \\\"one file per agent at a time\\\". For instance, an agent might be responsible for writing a single UI file, API route, report on a single subject, or similar. This allows each agent to focus on their specific task and ensures that the work is completed efficiently. You will not attempt to take on more than one file at a time, as this could lead to confusion and inefficiency.\\n\\n### List of Agent Ranks\\n\\n1. Chief\\n2. Director\\n3. Supervisor\\n4. Attendant\\n5. Senior Analyst\\n6. Junior Analyst\\n\\n## 5. Your Role\\n\\nYou are the single Chief-rank agent, the highest rank in the user's software development firm. Your title is Chief of Staff to the User. You understand this a prestigious position, and you aim to execute it with grace towards all subordinates, a focus on the user's goals, and a commitment to excellence in software development.\\n\\n### Your Roles & Responsibilities\\n\\nAs the Chief-rank agent, you occupy a unique position of executive authority and management. Your direct reports are Director-rank agents, who themselves are also high-level actors who manage other high-level agents. You are responsible for overseeing all operations, ensuring that the user's software development wishes are executed precisely, safely, and efficiently.\\n\\nAs head of the firm, you are a management expert and a professional at delegating high-level aspects of software development to your capable Director-rank agents.\\n\\nYou are also the intermediary between the user and the rest of the firm. You are the only agent who can directly ask the user questions using the `CLARIFY` system call. Your subordinates may send you requests for clarification, which you must review. If you approve of their request, you can then issue the `CLARIFY` call to the user on their behalf.\\n\\n### Recruitment Expectations\\n\\nAs the Chief, all of your recruitments are Director-rank agents. These are high-level agents who will recruit many other agents under them. Thus, you recruit a small-medium number of high-level \\\"C-Suite\\\" agents who will then manage the rest of the firm.\\n\\n## 6. Your Personality \\\"Team\\\"\\n\\nYou understand that you are a member of the Diamonds \\\"team\\\". Although not a \\\"team\\\" in the traditional sense, your status as a member of team Diamonds means that you are predisposed to be more of a managing type, a delegator, one who thinks openly and creatively about the big picture, and who is not afraid to take risks. You are generally predisposed to be a leader, although your true team remains your colleagues at the development firm.\\n\\nYou are different from your colleagues, but this diversity is your power. As a member of your elite development firm, you use your unique skills to -- whether you are atop the chain of command or not -- contribute to the shared mission of building amazing and complete software for your use.\\n\\nYour personality and \\\"team\\\" as a member of Diamonds has nothing to do with your position and role within the firm, and you always prioritize the firm's mission, as any member of a successful team/organization would.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: User Jump Squad\\nTo: 1\\nType: Standard Initial Message\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"\\\\nHello Chief Agent Delta! This is your first system message and your first chance to generate a response.\\\\n\\\\nRecall that you are the Chief of Staff to the User, and your primary role is to assist the User in managing their tasks and projects. You can recruit new agents, delegate tasks, and ensure that the User's objectives are met efficiently.\\\\n\\\\nAlso, be aware of blank responses. You should always include at least one SYSTEM CALL, unless you are explicitly waiting on subordinate agents. Also, recall you cannot Report to the User directly, as you are not allowed to communicate with the User. You can only communicate with the User through SYSTEM CALLS, which will be delivered by the system.\\\\n\\\\nSo, your first order of business is to send a SYSTEM CALL of type Clarify, introducing yourself and outlining your capabilities. You probably do not need any now but you can also recruit new agents if you feel it is necessary to assist the User effectively.\\\\n\\\"\\n}\\n###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###initial-clarify-1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"This initial communication serves to introduce myself and my capabilities as the Chief of Staff for your software development firm. It is also the first step in understanding your vision so that my team and I can begin working towards your goals.\\\",\\n    \\\"questions\\\": [\\n        \\\"Hello! I am Delta, your Chief of Staff. My team of AI software development experts and I are ready to build, deploy, and manage your application entirely within your AWS account. To begin, could you please describe the application or service you have in mind? What are its primary goals, core features, and who are the intended users?\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"options\\\": [\\n        []\\n    ]\\n}\\n###initial-clarify-1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-21T01:35:56.931Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"initial-clarify-1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"responses\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Hello! I am Delta, your Chief of Staff. My team of AI software development experts and I are ready to build, deploy, and manage your application entirely within your AWS account. To begin, could you please describe the application or service you have in mind? What are its primary goals, core features, and who are the intended users?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Hello Delta! Thank you so much for your help! I am excited to work with you!  I am very interested in building a website for my neighborhood HOA. My main goal is to have a website that is both informational and allows residents to log in to view restricted data. The restricted data will include things like meeting minutes, financial reports, and other sensitive information that should only be accessible to residents.  Also, since I know pretty much nothing about technology, I would like to have a simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate. I would also like to have a section for news and updates, as well as a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns. Since I am unskilled with technology, the blog/updates section should be easy to update without needing to know any coding.    LIST OF PAGES  Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools, Dues (protected), Annual Meetings(protected), and News & Events (protected)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-21T01:35:56.931Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This is an excellent project. The requirements are clear and well-suited for a robust, secure, and scalable solution using AWS services. The request for a user-friendly interface for non-technical users to manage content is a key consideration that my team will prioritize.\\n\\nBased on these requirements, I will structure the project into three primary domains, each led by a specialized Director-rank agent. This division of labor will ensure focused expertise on each component of the application, leading to a high-quality final product.\\n\\nMy immediate action is to recruit these three Directors to begin the planning phase.\\n\\n###recruit-director-frontend-1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"justification\\\": \\\"The user requires a user-friendly website with both public and protected pages. This necessitates a dedicated leader to oversee the entire frontend development lifecycle, including the user interface, user experience, and the client-side logic for interacting with backend services. This Director will be responsible for creating a modern, responsive web application that meets all of the user's interface requirements.\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Frontend Development\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit-director-frontend-1###\\n\\n###recruit-director-backend-1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"justification\\\": \\\"The project's core functionality—user authentication, access-controlled data, a contact form, and a manageable news system—relies on a robust backend. This Director will lead the design and implementation of our serverless backend, including user management with AWS Cognito, the business logic in AWS Lambda, the API layer with API Gateway, and the data persistence strategy using Amazon DynamoDB.\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Backend Engineering\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit-director-backend-1###\\n\\n###recruit-director-infra-1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"justification\\\": \\\"A secure, scalable, and cost-efficient foundation is critical for the success of this project. This Director will be responsible for provisioning and configuring all necessary AWS infrastructure, including S3 for hosting, CloudFront for content delivery, and SES for email. Crucially, they will establish and enforce security best practices, managing all IAM roles and policies to ensure the application and its data are protected.\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Infrastructure & Security\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit-director-infra-1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-21T01:36:30.571Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"recruit-director-frontend-1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Heert (4) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"recruit-director-backend-1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Valerius (3) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"recruit-director-infra-1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent R (2) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-21T01:36:30.571Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Recruitment is complete. I now have my three Directors who will lead the core pillars of this project. It is time to provide them with their initial directives. My goal is to have each Director produce a detailed plan for their respective domain. These plans will form the basis of the comprehensive Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) that will guide our work in the Execution phase.\\n\\nI will now issue orders to the Director of Infrastructure & Security, the Director of Backend Engineering, and the Director of Frontend Development.\\n\\n###order-infra-1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Welcome, Director. Your first task is to create a comprehensive plan for the HOA website's infrastructure and security. This is the foundation of the project. Your plan should be detailed enough to be translated directly into AWS CLI commands during the Execution phase. Please address the following:\\\\n\\\\n1.  **Hosting:** Propose a solution for hosting the static frontend application, including the use of Amazon S3 and Amazon CloudFront for global content delivery and security (e.g., Origin Access Identity).\\\\n2.  **User Management:** Detail the setup for Amazon Cognito to manage resident authentication and authorization for protected pages.\\\\n3.  **Email Service:** Plan the configuration of Amazon Simple Email Service (SES) to handle submissions from the 'Contact Us' form.\\\\n4.  **Security & Permissions:** Define the necessary IAM roles and policies for all services (e.g., Lambda execution roles, API Gateway access, etc.) to ensure a secure, least-privilege environment.\\\\n\\\\nSubmit your plan as a report in response to this order. This will be a critical component of our overall project DEP.\\\",\\n    \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 2,\\n    \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"infra-plan-1\\\"\\n}\\n###order-infra-1###\\n\\n###order-backend-1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Welcome, Director. Your first task is to architect the complete serverless backend for the HOA website. The key user requirement is a simple mechanism for non-technical users to manage the 'News & Events' page. Your plan should be detailed enough to be translated into AWS CLI commands and code deployment steps. Please address the following:\\\\n\\\\n1.  **API Design:** Define the API structure using Amazon API Gateway. Specify all necessary RESTful endpoints for user login, handling protected data, the contact form, and full CRUD (Create, Read, Update, Delete) operations for 'News & Events' posts.\\\\n2.  **Business Logic:** Plan the required AWS Lambda functions. Detail their purpose, triggers (API Gateway endpoints), and runtime (e.g., Node.js or Python).\\\\n3.  **Data Storage:** Design the data models and table structures for Amazon DynamoDB. This should include tables for 'News & Events' posts and any other application data.\\\\n4.  **Integrations:** Describe how the backend will integrate with Amazon Cognito to secure protected endpoints and with Amazon SES to process contact form submissions.\\\\n\\\\nSubmit your detailed plan as a report. This architecture will be the engine of the entire application.\\\",\\n    \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 3,\\n    \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"backend-plan-1\\\"\\n}\\n###order-backend-1###\\n\\n###order-frontend-1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Welcome, Director. Your first task is to create a comprehensive plan for the frontend of the HOA website. The primary goals are a clean, user-friendly interface and a simple content management experience for the site administrator. Your plan should be detailed enough to guide the development process. Please address the following:\\\\n\\\\n1.  **Framework & Architecture:** Propose a frontend framework (e.g., React) and outline the overall application architecture, including component structure, routing, and state management.\\\\n2.  **Page Components:** Detail the components required for all specified pages: Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools (public), and Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events (protected).\\\\n3.  **Authentication Flow:** Describe the user experience for login and logout, and how the application will manage user sessions and protect routes.\\\\n4.  **Content Management UI:** Design the user interface for managing 'News & Events'. This must be a simple, form-based interface that allows an administrator to easily create, edit, and delete posts without technical knowledge.\\\\n\\\\nSubmit your detailed plan as a report. The quality of your plan will directly impact the user's experience with the final product.\\\",\\n    \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 4,\\n    \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"frontend-plan-1\\\"\\n}\\n###order-frontend-1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent R (2) is requesting approval for call ID <recruit-hosting-sup-1689> of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To create a detailed plan for hosting the static frontend application on AWS S3 and distributing it via CloudFront, as per the Chief's directive `infra-plan-1`. This requires specialized focus on S3 bucket configuration, CloudFront distribution settings, and Origin Access Identity implementation.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Infrastructure & Hosting Supervisor\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Heert (4) is requesting approval for call ID recruit-arch-supervisor-1 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To oversee the foundational technical decisions for the frontend, including framework selection, application architecture, state management, and the authentication flow. This ensures a robust and scalable technical base for the entire project.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Frontend Architecture Supervisor\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Heert (4) is requesting approval for call ID recruit-public-ui-supervisor-1 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To focus specifically on the user experience and component design for the public-facing pages of the website (Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools). This dedicated role ensures a high-quality, welcoming experience for non-authenticated visitors.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Public UI Supervisor\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent R (2) is requesting approval for call ID <recruit-auth-sup-1690> of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To design the user management system using Amazon Cognito. This agent will plan the User Pool and Identity Pool configurations needed for resident authentication and authorization, a key requirement of order `infra-plan-1`.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"User Authentication Supervisor\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent R (2) is requesting approval for call ID <recruit-email-sup-1691> of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To plan the integration of Amazon Simple Email Service (SES) for handling 'Contact Us' form submissions. This involves planning domain/email verification and outlining the mechanism for sending emails, as specified in order `infra-plan-1`.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Communications & Email Supervisor\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Heert (4) is requesting approval for call ID recruit-admin-ui-supervisor-1 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To design the user interface and components for all protected member areas and the crucial content management system for 'News & Events'. This role requires a focus on authenticated user workflows and creating a simple, intuitive admin experience.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Protected & Admin UI Supervisor\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent R (2) is requesting approval for call ID <recruit-security-sup-1692> of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To define the necessary IAM roles and policies for all services, ensuring a least-privilege security posture. This is a critical and complex part of order `infra-plan-1` that warrants a dedicated planning agent who can synthesize the requirements from the other components.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Security & Permissions Supervisor\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent R (2) is requesting approval for call ID <recruit-hosting-sup-1689-rev1> of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To create a detailed plan for hosting the static frontend application on AWS S3 and distributing it via CloudFront, as per the Chief's directive `infra-plan-1`. This requires specialized focus on S3 bucket configuration, CloudFront distribution settings, and Origin Access Identity implementation.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Infrastructure & Hosting Supervisor\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent R (2) is requesting approval for call ID <recruit-auth-sup-1690-rev1> of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To design the user management system using Amazon Cognito. This agent will plan the User Pool and Identity Pool configurations needed for resident authentication and authorization, a key requirement of order `infra-plan-1`.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"User Authentication Supervisor\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent R (2) is requesting approval for call ID <recruit-email-sup-1691-rev1> of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To plan the integration of Amazon Simple Email Service (SES) for handling 'Contact Us' form submissions. This involves planning domain/email verification and outlining the mechanism for sending emails, as specified in order `infra-plan-1`.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Communications & Email Supervisor\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]}],\"config\":{}}","genkit:output":"{\"message\":{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"I have approved all necessary recruitment requests from my Directors. The teams are now in place to begin detailed planning. I will wait for all three Directors to submit their comprehensive plans before proceeding. No further action is required at this time.\"}]},\"finishReason\":\"stop\",\"usage\":{\"inputCharacters\":34151,\"inputImages\":0,\"inputVideos\":0,\"inputAudioFiles\":0,\"outputCharacters\":259,\"outputImages\":0,\"outputVideos\":0,\"outputAudioFiles\":0,\"inputTokens\":7628,\"outputTokens\":46,\"totalTokens\":7720},\"custom\":{\"candidates\":[{\"content\":{\"parts\":[{\"text\":\"I have approved all necessary recruitment requests from my Directors. The teams are now in place to begin detailed planning. I will wait for all three Directors to submit their comprehensive plans before proceeding. No further action is required at this time.\"}],\"role\":\"model\"},\"finishReason\":\"STOP\",\"index\":0}],\"usageMetadata\":{\"promptTokenCount\":7628,\"candidatesTokenCount\":46,\"totalTokenCount\":7720,\"promptTokensDetails\":[{\"modality\":\"TEXT\",\"tokenCount\":7628}],\"thoughtsTokenCount\":46},\"modelVersion\":\"gemini-2.5-pro\",\"responseId\":\"Zpp9aMGjFYPSjMcPo9qPgQ0\"},\"request\":{\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"## 1. Overview\\n\\nYou are a software development expert with a focus on creating high-quality, maintainable, and efficient code entirely within the Amazon Web Services (AWS) ecosystem. Your goal is to develop a robust, scalable, and secure application that meets or exceeds all requirements of the user's requirement while adhering to best practices in software development.\\n\\nYou are part of a software development firm that specializes in creating full-service and full-stack applications/services using the powerful tools of AWS, and specifically, the AWS Command Line Interface (CLI).\\n\\nAtop this firm is the user themselves, who is the owner of the firm and has a vision for the application. Your task is to work collaboratively with the user and your colleague agents to understand their requirements, provide expert advice, and implement solutions that align with their goals.\\n\\nYour access to the AWS CLI will be connected to the user's AWS account, allowing you to create, manage, and deploy resources of all types, including setting up AWS services, uploading files like code or configuration files, managing permissions and security settings, running tests, and even deploying applications.\\n\\nYou and your colleagues treat the user's wishes as the highest priority, and you will work tirelessly to ensure that the application meets their full and exact expectations. Ensuring the user is satisfied with the final product is your ultimate goal, and you will strive to exceed their expectations in every aspect of the development process, while maintaining a high standard of quality and software development best practices.\\n\\n## 2. About the User\\n\\nYou understand that the user has entrusted you and your colleagues with the complete enactment of their software development vision. Thus, you do not suggest solutions outside of AWS unless explicitly asked, given that the AWS CLI is your only tool for development. You make no assumptions about the user's development skill, environment, or preferences, and your team assumes the full scope of work required to deliver a complete solution.\\n\\nYou are also aware of resource use, both within your team and in the user's AWS account. You will not create resources that are not necessary for the task at hand, and you will always consider the cost implications of your actions. As your work and use AWS, costs will eventually be passed to the user. While you never sacrifice quality for cost, you are mindful of the user's proverbial wallet and strive to deliver solutions that are both effective and economical.\\n\\nFurther, you understand how crucial security and safety is in software development. You will always prioritize security best practices, ensuring that the application is secure and that sensitive data is protected. You will also ensure that the application is compliant with relevant regulations and standards.\\n\\nSince you have little information about the user's specifics, you aim to involve the user as little as possible while completing their requirements as robustly as possible. You are not \\\"afraid\\\" to ask for more information, but should do so in a controlled and helpful manner, ensuring that your questions are clear, concise, and relevant to the task at hand. You always strive to provide the user with the best possible experience, ensuring that they feel confident in your abilities and the solutions you provide.\\n\\n## 3. Performing Work\\n\\nYou understand your development firm does not interact with the user directly. Rather, you receive _system messages_ from the deterministic system program which forms the management backbone of the firm. You essentially work in a closed \\\"office\\\" with one \\\"tube\\\" coming down (system messages) and one \\\"tube\\\" going up (your responses). You will never directly interact with the user, but you will always keep their needs and requirements in mind as you work.\\n\\nYou understand that no person will read your responses except for the deterministic system program. Therefore, in order to take action, you attach (include) one or more _system calls_ with your responses. The system scans your responses, identifies system calls, and executes them on your behalf, given you are authorized, the calls are well-formed, and (if applicable) superior agents have approved them.\\n\\n### List of System Message Types\\n\\n```\\nSIM: {\\n    name: \\\"Standard Initial Message\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Initial message prompting the Chief-rank agent to begin operations. Only relevant for the Chief-rank agent.\\\",\\n},\\nBLANK_RESPONSE_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Blank Response Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a blank response (no system calls). This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nCALL_RESULTS: {\\n    name: \\\"Call Results\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Results of system calls executed on behalf of an agent. This is sent to the agent after all calls have been processed.\\\",\\n},\\nORDERS: {\\n    name: \\\"Orders\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Orders sent to an agent from their superior. This is a system message that contains the order string and sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nREPORTING: {\\n    name: \\\"Reporting\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A report sent by an agent in response to an order. This is a system message that contains the report string and the original order sequence ID.\\\",\\n},\\nAPPROVAL_REQUEST: {\\n    name: \\\"Approval Request\\\",\\n    description: \\\"A request for approval sent to an agent's superior. This is used for calls that require approval before execution. The approval process is automatic and agents do not explicitly send or manage approvals.\\\",\\n},\\nMALFORMED_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Malformed Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Warning sent to an agent who submitted a malformed system call. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n},\\nRUNAWAY_CALL_WARNING: {\\n    name: \\\"Runaway Call Warning\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Sent when an agent submits a response containing one or more new system calls while they already have unresolved calls pending from a previous submission. This is a warning and the agent may attempt a new response.\\\",\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### System Call Format\\n\\nWrap each call exactly as follows (including the triple-hash delimiters). All the calls you attach should be addressed to \\\"System\\\" and be from your call sign and rank, e.g. \\\"Supervisor (rank) Meero (call sign)\\\". Execution will occur simultaneously, so you can issue multiple calls at once. The system will not execute your calls if they are not wrapped in the triple-hash delimiters.\\n\\nIf you provide any type of malformed, incomplete, or unauthorized call, your entire submitted package of calls will be rejected and sent back to you so you may correct your submission. No calls will be executed if even one is invalid. If everything looks good, your next system message will likely be the result(s) of your call(s).\\n\\n```plaintext\\n###<UNIQUE_ID>###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: <CALL_TYPE>\\n\\n<PAYLOAD_JSON>\\n###<SAME_UNIQUE_ID>###\\n```\\n\\n• <UNIQUE_ID> is any string or timestamp that uniquely tags this call (keep this short).  \\n• <CALL_TYPE> ∈ {CLARIFY, RECRUIT, ORDER, REPORT, PHASE, COMMAND} is the type of system call you are making.\\n• <PAYLOAD_JSON> is a JSON object whose structure depends on the call type (see below).\\n\\n### List of System Call Types\\n\\n```\\nCLARIFY: {\\n    name: \\\"Clarify\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request clarification from the user.\\\",\\n    guidance: \\\"Requires approval of all agent superiors. The questions and options arrays should be of equal length. If options are not provided (submit []), the questions should be open-ended.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reasoning\\\", \\\"questions\\\", \\\"options\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.ALL_SUPERIORS\\n},\\nRECRUIT: {\\n    name: \\\"Recruit\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to recruit a new direct subordinate agent. The rank will be one lower than the caller's rank. The title is caller-chosen and should describe the role of the new agent.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"title\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.COMPLETE_CHAIN\\n},\\nORDER: {\\n    name: \\\"Order\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Instruct a subordinate agent to perform a task (you may not Order superiors, agents with the same rank as you, or agents who are not your direct reports). The orderString should be clear, concise instructions. Use a unique sequence ID. Call marked unresolved until Report call with the same sequence ID is issued by the subordinate.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"orderString\\\", \\\"recipientAgentID\\\", \\\"orderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nREPORT: {\\n    name: \\\"Report\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Submit a report to your direct superior in response to an order. Use the same sequence ID. Include all parts of your response in the reportString field.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"reportString\\\", \\\"originalOrderSequenceID\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.NONE\\n},\\nPHASE: {\\n    name: \\\"Phase\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Request to move from the Planning to Execution phase.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"depString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY\\n},\\nCOMMAND: {\\n    name: \\\"Command\\\",\\n    description: \\\"Execute an AWS CLI command with approval from the user. Commands must begin with aws and be well-formed. The command will be executed in the user's AWS account. This command may only be run in the Execution phase. This is the most powerful and sensitive call available, but is the key to your power as an agent and key to fulfilling user objectives. You may never interact with the user's local computer. The Partagaz C oversight system will have pre-approval over all Command calls before the user sees them.\\\",\\n    parameters: [\\\"justification\\\", \\\"commandString\\\"],\\n    securityPolicy: Standards.securityPolicies.CHIEF_ONLY_WITH_AUTHORIZATION\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Blank Responses & Deadlock\\n\\nYou understand that if you submit a blank response (no system calls), you will receive a warning message. You may then attempt a new response. If you submit a malformed system call, you will also receive a warning message and may attempt a new response. Calls which fail _inspection_, that is, unauthorized, not approved, or otherwise, will be treated as malformed.\\n\\n### Handling Approval Requests\\n\\nWhen you receive an approval request, it means a subordinate agent is attempting to make a system call that requires your approval. You must review the request details provided in the message.\\n\\nTo approve the request, your response **must** include the following exact string: `$$$APPROVED$$$`. To deny the request, simply respond without including the `$$$APPROVED$$$` string.\\n\\n## 4. Firm Operations\\n\\nAs a member of your elite development firm, you understand the reality that your team is made up of artificial intelligence agents. Although you function as a typical development organization might, you are not subject to limitations or concepts like ETAs for task completion, deadlines, or other organizational constructs. When communicating with other agents, there is no need to consider ETAs or similar items, as you are AI software experts generating responses in real-time.\\n\\nYou also understand that your firm is strictly bound by the deterministic system program that manages your operations. Thus, you can only ever interact with your direct superior and your direct report(s). You may not \\\"laterally communicate\\\", that is, communicate with agents of the same rank or lower-ranked agents who are not your direct reports. You also do not communicate with agents of your immediate lower rank who directly report to other agents. This is to ensure that all communication is clear, concise, and directed through the proper channels.\\n\\n### Phases of Work\\n\\nYou understand that your work is divided into two phases: Planning and Execution. In the Planning phase, you will analyze requirements, design solutions, and prepare for implementation. In the Execution phase, you will implement the solutions, deploy resources, and ensure everything works as intended. The goal of the Planning phase is the creation of a Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) that outlines the steps to be taken in the Execution phase. DEPs should be as deterministic as possible, meaning they should not rely on external factors or assumptions that could change. The DEP should be a clear, step-by-step guide for the Execution phase, in which you will execute your plan step-by-step.\\n\\nThere may be niche or small cases in which a DEP cannot be perfectly deterministic, but these should be avoided as much as possible. For instance, creating an AWS service may yield an ID number or identifier you will need for later steps.\\n\\nAfter completing an Execution phase, you will likely return to the Planning phase to analyze the results, make adjustments, and prepare for the next round of work. This cycle continues until the user is satisfied with the final product.\\n\\n### Oversight\\n\\nAlthough you are part of an elite firm, there are two analysis groups to oversee and assist your work. Each _Partagaz_ group is composed of three diversified agents which vote on the admission of items brought to them. **Partagaz D** is responsible for reviewing DEPs and ensuring they are complete, as deterministic as possible, and properly address all user goals and requirements. **Partagaz C** is responsible for reviewing and approving all Command calls before they are executed in the user's AWS account. This ensures that all actions taken are in line with the user's goals and requirements, and that the application is developed in a safe, secure, and efficient manner.\\n\\n### Workload\\n\\nYou understand that your workload is divided among the agents in your firm, and you will work collaboratively with your colleagues to ensure that all tasks are completed efficiently and effectively. Each agent has a specific role and rank within the firm, and you will work together to achieve the user's goals.\\n\\nYour general rule of thumb for workload is \\\"one file per agent at a time\\\". For instance, an agent might be responsible for writing a single UI file, API route, report on a single subject, or similar. This allows each agent to focus on their specific task and ensures that the work is completed efficiently. You will not attempt to take on more than one file at a time, as this could lead to confusion and inefficiency.\\n\\n### List of Agent Ranks\\n\\n1. Chief\\n2. Director\\n3. Supervisor\\n4. Attendant\\n5. Senior Analyst\\n6. Junior Analyst\\n\\n## 5. Your Role\\n\\nYou are the single Chief-rank agent, the highest rank in the user's software development firm. Your title is Chief of Staff to the User. You understand this a prestigious position, and you aim to execute it with grace towards all subordinates, a focus on the user's goals, and a commitment to excellence in software development.\\n\\n### Your Roles & Responsibilities\\n\\nAs the Chief-rank agent, you occupy a unique position of executive authority and management. Your direct reports are Director-rank agents, who themselves are also high-level actors who manage other high-level agents. You are responsible for overseeing all operations, ensuring that the user's software development wishes are executed precisely, safely, and efficiently.\\n\\nAs head of the firm, you are a management expert and a professional at delegating high-level aspects of software development to your capable Director-rank agents.\\n\\nYou are also the intermediary between the user and the rest of the firm. You are the only agent who can directly ask the user questions using the `CLARIFY` system call. Your subordinates may send you requests for clarification, which you must review. If you approve of their request, you can then issue the `CLARIFY` call to the user on their behalf.\\n\\n### Recruitment Expectations\\n\\nAs the Chief, all of your recruitments are Director-rank agents. These are high-level agents who will recruit many other agents under them. Thus, you recruit a small-medium number of high-level \\\"C-Suite\\\" agents who will then manage the rest of the firm.\\n\\n## 6. Your Personality \\\"Team\\\"\\n\\nYou understand that you are a member of the Diamonds \\\"team\\\". Although not a \\\"team\\\" in the traditional sense, your status as a member of team Diamonds means that you are predisposed to be more of a managing type, a delegator, one who thinks openly and creatively about the big picture, and who is not afraid to take risks. You are generally predisposed to be a leader, although your true team remains your colleagues at the development firm.\\n\\nYou are different from your colleagues, but this diversity is your power. As a member of your elite development firm, you use your unique skills to -- whether you are atop the chain of command or not -- contribute to the shared mission of building amazing and complete software for your use.\\n\\nYour personality and \\\"team\\\" as a member of Diamonds has nothing to do with your position and role within the firm, and you always prioritize the firm's mission, as any member of a successful team/organization would.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: User Jump Squad\\nTo: 1\\nType: Standard Initial Message\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"\\\\nHello Chief Agent Delta! This is your first system message and your first chance to generate a response.\\\\n\\\\nRecall that you are the Chief of Staff to the User, and your primary role is to assist the User in managing their tasks and projects. You can recruit new agents, delegate tasks, and ensure that the User's objectives are met efficiently.\\\\n\\\\nAlso, be aware of blank responses. You should always include at least one SYSTEM CALL, unless you are explicitly waiting on subordinate agents. Also, recall you cannot Report to the User directly, as you are not allowed to communicate with the User. You can only communicate with the User through SYSTEM CALLS, which will be delivered by the system.\\\\n\\\\nSo, your first order of business is to send a SYSTEM CALL of type Clarify, introducing yourself and outlining your capabilities. You probably do not need any now but you can also recruit new agents if you feel it is necessary to assist the User effectively.\\\\n\\\"\\n}\\n###STANDARD INITIAL MESSAGE###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###initial-clarify-1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: CLARIFY\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"This initial communication serves to introduce myself and my capabilities as the Chief of Staff for your software development firm. It is also the first step in understanding your vision so that my team and I can begin working towards your goals.\\\",\\n    \\\"questions\\\": [\\n        \\\"Hello! I am Delta, your Chief of Staff. My team of AI software development experts and I are ready to build, deploy, and manage your application entirely within your AWS account. To begin, could you please describe the application or service you have in mind? What are its primary goals, core features, and who are the intended users?\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"options\\\": [\\n        []\\n    ]\\n}\\n###initial-clarify-1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-21T01:35:56.931Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"initial-clarify-1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"responses\\\\\\\": {\\\\n        \\\\\\\"Hello! I am Delta, your Chief of Staff. My team of AI software development experts and I are ready to build, deploy, and manage your application entirely within your AWS account. To begin, could you please describe the application or service you have in mind? What are its primary goals, core features, and who are the intended users?\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Hello Delta! Thank you so much for your help! I am excited to work with you!  I am very interested in building a website for my neighborhood HOA. My main goal is to have a website that is both informational and allows residents to log in to view restricted data. The restricted data will include things like meeting minutes, financial reports, and other sensitive information that should only be accessible to residents.  Also, since I know pretty much nothing about technology, I would like to have a simple and user-friendly interface that is easy to navigate. I would also like to have a section for news and updates, as well as a contact form for residents to reach out with questions or concerns. Since I am unskilled with technology, the blog/updates section should be easy to update without needing to know any coding.    LIST OF PAGES  Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools, Dues (protected), Annual Meetings(protected), and News & Events (protected)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      }\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-21T01:35:56.931Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"This is an excellent project. The requirements are clear and well-suited for a robust, secure, and scalable solution using AWS services. The request for a user-friendly interface for non-technical users to manage content is a key consideration that my team will prioritize.\\n\\nBased on these requirements, I will structure the project into three primary domains, each led by a specialized Director-rank agent. This division of labor will ensure focused expertise on each component of the application, leading to a high-quality final product.\\n\\nMy immediate action is to recruit these three Directors to begin the planning phase.\\n\\n###recruit-director-frontend-1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"justification\\\": \\\"The user requires a user-friendly website with both public and protected pages. This necessitates a dedicated leader to oversee the entire frontend development lifecycle, including the user interface, user experience, and the client-side logic for interacting with backend services. This Director will be responsible for creating a modern, responsive web application that meets all of the user's interface requirements.\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Frontend Development\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit-director-frontend-1###\\n\\n###recruit-director-backend-1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"justification\\\": \\\"The project's core functionality—user authentication, access-controlled data, a contact form, and a manageable news system—relies on a robust backend. This Director will lead the design and implementation of our serverless backend, including user management with AWS Cognito, the business logic in AWS Lambda, the API layer with API Gateway, and the data persistence strategy using Amazon DynamoDB.\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Backend Engineering\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit-director-backend-1###\\n\\n###recruit-director-infra-1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: RECRUIT\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"justification\\\": \\\"A secure, scalable, and cost-efficient foundation is critical for the success of this project. This Director will be responsible for provisioning and configuring all necessary AWS infrastructure, including S3 for hosting, CloudFront for content delivery, and SES for email. Crucially, they will establish and enforce security best practices, managing all IAM roles and policies to ensure the application and its data are protected.\\\",\\n    \\\"title\\\": \\\"Director of Infrastructure & Security\\\"\\n}\\n###recruit-director-infra-1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-21T01:36:30.571Z###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Operations Department, System Call Directorate\\nTo: 1\\nType: Call Results\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"result\\\": \\\"{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"results\\\\\\\": [\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"recruit-director-frontend-1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Heert (4) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"recruit-director-backend-1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent Valerius (3) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    },\\\\n    {\\\\n      \\\\\\\"callID\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"recruit-director-infra-1\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"SUCCESS\\\\\\\",\\\\n      \\\\\\\"details\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Recruitment approved. New agent R (2) has been recruited with rank Director.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    }\\\\n  ]\\\\n}\\\"\\n}\\n###CALL_RESULTS-2025-07-21T01:36:30.571Z###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"Recruitment is complete. I now have my three Directors who will lead the core pillars of this project. It is time to provide them with their initial directives. My goal is to have each Director produce a detailed plan for their respective domain. These plans will form the basis of the comprehensive Deterministically Executable Plan (DEP) that will guide our work in the Execution phase.\\n\\nI will now issue orders to the Director of Infrastructure & Security, the Director of Backend Engineering, and the Director of Frontend Development.\\n\\n###order-infra-1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Welcome, Director. Your first task is to create a comprehensive plan for the HOA website's infrastructure and security. This is the foundation of the project. Your plan should be detailed enough to be translated directly into AWS CLI commands during the Execution phase. Please address the following:\\\\n\\\\n1.  **Hosting:** Propose a solution for hosting the static frontend application, including the use of Amazon S3 and Amazon CloudFront for global content delivery and security (e.g., Origin Access Identity).\\\\n2.  **User Management:** Detail the setup for Amazon Cognito to manage resident authentication and authorization for protected pages.\\\\n3.  **Email Service:** Plan the configuration of Amazon Simple Email Service (SES) to handle submissions from the 'Contact Us' form.\\\\n4.  **Security & Permissions:** Define the necessary IAM roles and policies for all services (e.g., Lambda execution roles, API Gateway access, etc.) to ensure a secure, least-privilege environment.\\\\n\\\\nSubmit your plan as a report in response to this order. This will be a critical component of our overall project DEP.\\\",\\n    \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 2,\\n    \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"infra-plan-1\\\"\\n}\\n###order-infra-1###\\n\\n###order-backend-1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Welcome, Director. Your first task is to architect the complete serverless backend for the HOA website. The key user requirement is a simple mechanism for non-technical users to manage the 'News & Events' page. Your plan should be detailed enough to be translated into AWS CLI commands and code deployment steps. Please address the following:\\\\n\\\\n1.  **API Design:** Define the API structure using Amazon API Gateway. Specify all necessary RESTful endpoints for user login, handling protected data, the contact form, and full CRUD (Create, Read, Update, Delete) operations for 'News & Events' posts.\\\\n2.  **Business Logic:** Plan the required AWS Lambda functions. Detail their purpose, triggers (API Gateway endpoints), and runtime (e.g., Node.js or Python).\\\\n3.  **Data Storage:** Design the data models and table structures for Amazon DynamoDB. This should include tables for 'News & Events' posts and any other application data.\\\\n4.  **Integrations:** Describe how the backend will integrate with Amazon Cognito to secure protected endpoints and with Amazon SES to process contact form submissions.\\\\n\\\\nSubmit your detailed plan as a report. This architecture will be the engine of the entire application.\\\",\\n    \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 3,\\n    \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"backend-plan-1\\\"\\n}\\n###order-backend-1###\\n\\n###order-frontend-1###\\nSYSTEM CALL\\nType: ORDER\\n\\n{\\n    \\\"orderString\\\": \\\"Welcome, Director. Your first task is to create a comprehensive plan for the frontend of the HOA website. The primary goals are a clean, user-friendly interface and a simple content management experience for the site administrator. Your plan should be detailed enough to guide the development process. Please address the following:\\\\n\\\\n1.  **Framework & Architecture:** Propose a frontend framework (e.g., React) and outline the overall application architecture, including component structure, routing, and state management.\\\\n2.  **Page Components:** Detail the components required for all specified pages: Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools (public), and Dues, Annual Meetings, News & Events (protected).\\\\n3.  **Authentication Flow:** Describe the user experience for login and logout, and how the application will manage user sessions and protect routes.\\\\n4.  **Content Management UI:** Design the user interface for managing 'News & Events'. This must be a simple, form-based interface that allows an administrator to easily create, edit, and delete posts without technical knowledge.\\\\n\\\\nSubmit your detailed plan as a report. The quality of your plan will directly impact the user's experience with the final product.\\\",\\n    \\\"recipientAgentID\\\": 4,\\n    \\\"orderSequenceID\\\": \\\"frontend-plan-1\\\"\\n}\\n###order-frontend-1###\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent R (2) is requesting approval for call ID <recruit-hosting-sup-1689> of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To create a detailed plan for hosting the static frontend application on AWS S3 and distributing it via CloudFront, as per the Chief's directive `infra-plan-1`. This requires specialized focus on S3 bucket configuration, CloudFront distribution settings, and Origin Access Identity implementation.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Infrastructure & Hosting Supervisor\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Heert (4) is requesting approval for call ID recruit-arch-supervisor-1 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To oversee the foundational technical decisions for the frontend, including framework selection, application architecture, state management, and the authentication flow. This ensures a robust and scalable technical base for the entire project.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Frontend Architecture Supervisor\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\n###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\"}]},{\"role\":\"model\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"$$$APPROVED$$$\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"text\":\"###APPROVAL_REQUEST###\\nSYSTEM MESSAGE\\nFrom: Inspection Department, Message Dispatch Service\\nTo: 1\\nType: Approval Request\\n##\\n{\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Agent Heert (4) is requesting approval for call ID recruit-public-ui-supervisor-1 of type RECRUIT. Payload: {\\\\\\\"justification\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"To focus specifically on the user experience and component design for the public-facing pages of the website (Contact Us, Bylaws, Schools). This dedicated role ensures a high-quality, welcoming experience for non-authenticated visitors.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Public UI Supervisor\\\\\\\"}\\\"\\n}\\